    "vipSummary": {
      "id": 1448821611,
      "html": "<p>CYP3A4 is one of the key pharmacogenes involved in implementation of pharmacogenomics.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>It is involved in guidelines for quetiapine (<a href=\"/gene/PA131/prescribingInfo\">go to list of all guidelines with CYP3A4</a>).</li>\n<li>the nomenclature has been set by <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.pharmvar.org/gene/CYP3A4\" target=\"_blank\">PharmVar</a></li>\n<li>the AMP tier 1 allele is <a href=\"/haplotype/PA166048680\">CYP3A4*22</a> and tier 2 allele is <a href=\"/haplotype/PA165819244\">CYP3A4*20</a> <a href=\"/page/ampAllelesToTest\">see all alleles on the AMP recommended to test list</a>.</li>\n<li>key variant pages are <a href=\"/variant/PA166157487\">rs35599367</a> (defining for *22) and <a href=\"/variant/PA166157502\">rs67666821</a> (defining for *20).</li>\n<li>it is involved in many <a href=\"/gene/PA130/labelAnnotation\">drug label annotations</a> with a larger number of cautions for drug-drug interactions with CYP3A4 inhibitors (such as <a href=\"/chemical/PA450146\">ketoconazole</a>) and inducers (such as <a href=\"/chemical/PA448785\">carbamazepine</a>), see the <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://drug-interactions.medicine.iu.edu/MainTable.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">Flockhart table</a> for more CYP3A4 inhibitors, inducers and substrates.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "vipTier": "Tier 1"
  },
